# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# The Xcode project is generated from ios/project.yml by `mise run ios:gen`.
# Committing it would reintroduce exactly the pbxproj merge conflicts that
# choosing XcodeGen was meant to avoid.
ios/*.xcodeproj/
ios/*.xcworkspace/
# Also generated from project.yml — XcodeGen writes the target's Info.plist from
# its `info:` block. Committing it would leave two editable sources for one Info
# dictionary, where hand edits silently vanish on the next generate.
ios/Ond/Info.plist
ios/OndWatch/Info.plist
# Same again for the entitlements XcodeGen writes from each `entitlements:` block.
ios/Ond/Ond.entitlements
ios/OndWatch/OndWatch.entitlements
ios/**/.build/
# Xcode writes here whenever a build passes -derivedDataPath (mise run ios:build,
# check:diagrams). Object files and asset catalogues, hundreds of them, all
# untracked — enough to bury a `but status` and to get swept into a stray commit.
ios/**/build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# Secrets, and the per-machine Apple identifiers that behave like them. `.env`
# is loaded by .mise.toml so every task sees it, and every entry is optional —
# absent, the simulator still builds and the suite still runs, which is what CI
# and a fresh clone get. docs/contributing.md enumerates what goes in; listing
# them here too would be a second copy to fall out of step.
#
# Nothing beyond a secret or a value that genuinely differs per developer
# belongs in it (CLAUDE.md §1.4). The App Store Connect signing key is a file
# rather than a value, and lives under ~/.appstoreconnect/ — never in here.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Per-developer mise overrides — mise reads these automatically if present.
mise.local.toml
.mise.local.toml

# Agent scratch
/logs/
/tmp/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# vp needs a package.json at the root; nothing here installs dependencies, but
# a stray `pnpm dlx` can still leave this behind.
node_modules/
